      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Proactive AVX2 baseline selection and spawn error handling in CLI",
        "summary": "The CLI release wrapper now detects CPU AVX2 support up front on Windows (using PowerShell's IsProcessorFeaturePresent) and Linux (/proc/cpuinfo) instead of waiting for the optimized binary to crash with SIGILL, caching the result in `cpu-features.json` and routing to the `-baseline` target proactively. `spawnInstalledBinary` now wraps the spawn call in try/catch to handle synchronous spawn errors like Windows UNKNOWN errno from antivirus or Smart App Control, printing system info and a baseline override hint via the new `printSpawnFailure`/`exitOnSpawnFailure`. The staging banner log lines were removed from `cli/release-staging/index.js`, and `tree-sitter.wasm` ships as a sibling file to the binary during download. These changes span the codebuff, freebuff, and staging CLI release wrappers.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "All three files show the same AVX2 detection refactor: `linuxCpuHasAvx2` changed from a strict platform/arch guard (returning true for any non-linux-x64) to a try/catch reading `/proc/cpuinfo`; new `probeWindowsAvx2`, `machineHasAvx2`, `detectMachineHasAvx2`, `readCachedAvx2`, `writeCachedAvx2`, `getCpuFeatureCachePath`, `printBaselineOverrideHint`, and `printSystemInfo` functions were added to `cli/release-staging/index.js`, `cli/release/index.js`, and `freebuff/cli/release/index.js`; `getTargetOverride` now checks for missing spawn targets; `spawnInstalledBinary` wraps the spawn call in try/catch to handle synchronous spawn errors and `printSpawnFailure`/`exitOnSpawnFailure` were added; the staging banner log lines were removed; and `tree-sitter.wasm` is now moved as a sibling file to the binary during download in `cli/release/index.js` and `freebuff/cli/release/index.js`.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The rollout mechanism and whether the Windows AVX2 detection cache in `cpu-features.json` is cleared on uninstall.",
        "changes": [
          {
            "area": "cli/release-staging",
            "what": "Added proactive AVX2 CPU detection on Windows and Linux with disk caching, synchronous spawn error handling, and removed the staging banner log lines.",
