        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add freebuff-desktop-thread agent ID",
        "summary": "Added `FREEBUFF_DESKTOP_THREAD_AGENT_ID` ('freebuff-desktop-thread') to `common/src/constants/free-agents.ts`. This single root ID replaces per-model IDs for the desktop hosted harness, allowing the full desktop picker set. The agent is registered in `FREEBUFF_ROOT_AGENT_IDS` for abuse detection.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:04:57.788Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Freebuff Desktop now runs under a single shared account name for abuse tracking, the same way multiple web browser tabs can share one login, instead of needing a separate account name for each AI model you pick. If you use Freebuff Desktop and open several tabs with different models, the system still counts them as coming from one consistent source you, and the desktop tab you see in your picker now shows the full set of free models instead of being limited like the command-line version was. This is live today, so the change is already affecting how Freebuff Desktop sessions are recorded across all desktop users starting June30, 2026.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
