        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add referral signup window and limit constants",
        "summary": "Hoists `REFERRAL_SIGNUP_WINDOW_DAYS` (30) and `FREEBUFF_REFERRAL_SIGNUP_LIMIT` (100) into `common/src/constants/freebuff-referral-tiers.ts`. The window constant prevents attribution of pre-existing accounts by enforcing a 30-day post-signup limit. The signup limit acts as an anti-spam ceiling for `referral_v2` rows, preventing pathological row creation while leaving legitimate reward caps untouched.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:04:44.018Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If someone tries to claim a referral reward for an account that was created more than 30 days ago, the system will now reject it, a new cutoff makes sure referrers can only earn credit for genuinely recent signups. Separately, there's also a hard ceiling of 100 attributed referrals per person; this isn't a reward limit (those are already capped elsewhere) but a guardrail to stop automated abuse from creating thousands of fake referral records. Both limits are now baked into the shared referral logic, so the behavior is consistent whether you're signing up through the website, the CLI, or another entry point. It's live as part of the latest release.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
