        "at": "2026-09-14T16:03:09.511Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Behind the scenes in the agent runtime, the way the system turns a saved step template (written as text) into something the assistant can actually run has been tidied up into a single carefully labeled helper. If you were reading the logs while an agent ran, you might see the word 'deserializeHandleSteps' show up where 'eval' used to appear, but what the assistant does and how fast it does it stays the same. Nothing is live in a way you experience differently today; this is housekeeping that reduces the chance of a future mistake when building or modifying agent steps.",
